{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Summary\n- restore MCP App snapshots through the scoped result capability when a host omits standard toolInfo\n- retain that capability from both standard MCP events and ChatGPT compatibility metadata\n- treat empty compatibility and standard replay payloads as restore requests instead of rendering an empty card\n- preserve compatibility capabilities across later metadata-less empty standard replays\n- serialize capability, host-card, and disclosure-state saves so event ordering cannot move a snapshot backward\n- restore disclosure and pagination state before any initial ID-only save without replacing fresher displayed data\n- join concurrent restores for the same result before capability-backed persistence and fail closed when restore fails\n- preserve capability through metadata-less empty full-result replays and keep user interaction newer than restored view state\n- discard delayed historical restores after newer live output or a different host card identity arrives\n- preserve explicit ChatGPT null-output clears\n- avoid repeated snapshot RPCs for unrelated host-context changes or completed missing-result restores\n- bump the immutable app resource check to v11\n\n## Red to green\n- Red in production v10: event #3470748 rendered its JSON-template chart and table initially, then a full ChatGPT reload collapsed to an empty Lobu result; the snapshot row was never updated because no host card identity reached the iframe.\n- Red in focused review: empty preloaded compatibility output could block restore; compatibility-only metadata could lose or later erase the restore capability; delayed restore could overwrite newer live output or cross a host-card identity change; initial ID-only persistence could erase disclosure state; explicit null output could leave stale content visible; unrelated host-context events could repeat snapshot traffic; a concurrent, failed, or malformed replay restore could persist default state before restoration completed; an empty full-result replay could clear the only capability; delayed hydration could roll back a user interaction made before restore began; a non-empty standard replay could save empty disclosure state before restoring the capability-backed state; duplicate standard and compatibility deliveries could invalidate the shared restore; metadata arriving after cached widget data could skip view-state restoration; consecutive capability-only standard replays could retain the preceding card; out-of-sync inner and outer globals could merge a stale card or approval capability into a current result; a stale same-origin parent output could replace the current inner result; app-initiated results could retain the originating card identity; local disclosure or list pagination state could leak into the next result; a restored card could lend its capability and view state to different metadata-less live data; an app-initiated result could bind to a later host card; and a different capability-backed result could retain an unkeyed card identity and view state; a capability-only transition could keep stale unkeyed data; duplicate live data could cancel same-result ID-only hydration; and matching standard data could erase a pending capability restore./\n- Green: focused host suite 51\\/51, result-view suite 18/18, and compatibility parser suite 13/13, including empty-replay and compatibility-only result-boundary resets, capability-only save, preloaded and later compatibility restoration, explicit clear handling, metadata-less standard/full-result replay ordering, delayed toolInfo binding, initial view-state restore, local-interaction precedence, concurrent restore joining, restore-failure and malformed-response fail-closed behavior, overlapping view-state save serialization, data/identity stale-restore rejection, and snapshot RPC deduplication, and restore-before-save ordering for non-empty standard replays, overlapping standard/compatibility delivery, and metadata-after-cache restoration, completed-card identity replacement, explicit-clear precedence over late metadata, and merged hydration state without partial writes, split-target preload restoration, persistence after late identity restoration, and per-result view-state reset, consecutive capability-only replay switching, and cached-widget standard-capability restoration, cross-target stale-cache replacement, stale approval isolation, and split empty replay restoration, late host-identity enrichment during an in-flight capability restore, and app-initiated result capability retention, compatibility-first duplicate result delivery, capability-only restore persistence and late host-card binding, authoritative same-origin preload selection, app-result identity replacement, and local disclosure and list pagination reset.\n- Green: production MCP App bundle build and self-contained v11 resource check passed at 385,888 bytes.\n- Green: full Vitest suite passed across 156 files and 1,390 tests.\n- Green: TypeScript/build checks, targeted lint, and git diff check passed.\n\n## Safety\n- no visual redesign and no public tool surface change\n- the opaque per-result capability remains scoped to the private app helpers\n- real ChatGPT reload verification runs against the deployed parent after both PRs merge\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Improved restoration of app data, view state, and tool information after reconnecting or reopening an app.\n  - Added support for preserving app state when partial compatibility details are available.\n  - Improved handling of empty, replayed, or delayed tool results.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Prevented duplicate restore requests and stale results from overwriting newer live data.\n  - Improved reliability when restoring missing, invalid, or failed saved state.\n  - Preserved the latest app state during reconnects and host changes.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-08-11T02:10:20Z","authors":[{"email":"emrekabakci@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNzQ1","login":"buremba","name":"Burak Emre Kabakcı"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-11T09:12:25Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"fix(mcp-app): restore cards without host tool info","oid":"beee495568026e6454f315e1de9e15e67eac5dbe"}],"headRefName":"codex/mcp-app-capability-restore","number":795,"title":"fix(mcp-app): restore cards without host tool info"}

